{"id": "EUVD-2026-102331", "enisaUuid": "b090df23-93bc-3fb0-8eba-a4700347a229", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a newline injection vulnerability in services_pppoe_edit.php that allows privileged users to inject mpd.secret entries via unvalidated username POST fields. Attackers with the PPPoE Server Edit privilege can add a line whose secret begins with '!', making mpd5 run commands as root when a PPPoE client authenticates.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:11:33", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-pppoe-secret-bang", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/vpn.inc#L272-L282", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/services_pppoe_edit.php#L141-L152", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-command-injection-via-pppoe-server-username"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gg6q-95gx-p8r8", "CVE-2026-111219"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.87, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d7a75d81-3775-3b3b-814c-cb5bc6832c7b", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fcf9d40c-c1e3-32ab-9ea6-c8cd0862b84d", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}